---
// Home, direction 3 "Old Glory Modern" (A/B/C test arm, docs/AB_TEST.md). Layout and copy from
// FreeMyID-Design-Directions/3-old-glory-modern/landing.html; styles in styles/directions/glory.css.
// Copy rules: docs/POSITIONING.md (verified claims table), trust panel in the WO-162 short form (as Footer.astro).
// Every Download button goes through CtaDownload (D5). Zero client JS.
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import CtaDownload from "@/components/CtaDownload.astro";
import HomeFinePrint from "./HomeFinePrint.astro";
import { buttonVariants } from "@/components/ui/button-variants";
import { pageProps, url } from "@/lib/site";
const outline = buttonVariants({ variant: "onBrandOutline", size: "lg" });
const primary = buttonVariants({ variant: "primary", size: "lg" });
const star = "M12 2l2.9 6.9L22 9.3l-5.4 4.8L18.2 21 12 17.3 5.8 21l1.6-6.9L2 9.3l7.1-.4z";
const tick = "M5 12.5l4.5 4.5L19 7.5";
---
<Base {...pageProps("home")}>

<div class="home-wrap g-hero pt-l">
  <section class="g-panel" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="home-hero__text">
      {/* source: LICENSE (free); runs on your own computer = D8 / netpolicy.py */}
      <p class="g-pill"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d={star} /></svg>Free. Runs on your own computer.</p>
      {/* source: docs/POSITIONING.md "Take yourself off the market"; same line as the closing band of the current home */}
      <h1 id="hero-title" class="g-headline">Your information. Off the market.</h1>
      <p class="home-lead">Your name, address and phone number are for sale on people-search sites. Anyone can buy them. Free My ID asks those sites to take your details down, and keeps checking that they did.</p>
      <div class="home-actions">
        <CtaDownload look="onBrand" sub="Free for Windows 10 and 11" />
        <a class={outline} href={url("how-it-works/")}>See how it works</a>
      </div>
      <HomeFinePrint />
    </div>
    <div class="g-promise">
      <p class="g-promise__label">Our promise</p>
      <ul role="list">
        {["No account", "No cloud", "Free and open source", "Uninstall anytime"].map((t) => (
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d={tick} /></svg>{t}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      {/* Trust panel, current short form (WO-162, same as Footer.astro; docs/BRAND.md predates it) */}
      <p class="g-promise__note">No account. No cloud. Never asks for your Social Security number or bank or card details, and never charges you. Free and open source. Uninstall anytime.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<section class="home-band pt-0" aria-labelledby="post-title">
  <div class="home-wrap home-split">
    <div class="home-stack">
      <h2 id="post-title">That post went to the wrong place.</h2>
      {/* source: approved "the post" copy (pages/index.astro, i-do-not-consent page) */}
      <p>You may have shared an "I do not consent" post. The instinct was right. But the companies that sell your name, address and phone number never saw it.</p>
      <p>Free My ID takes that same "I do not consent" to the people-search sites themselves, through each site's own removal process, and keeps checking.</p>
      <p><a href={url("i-do-not-consent/")}>What the post can and can't do</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="g-compare">
      <div class="g-compare__item">
        <span class="g-compare__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><rect x="4" y="5" width="16" height="14" rx="2" /><path d="M8 10h8M8 14h5" /></svg></span>
        <div><p class="g-compare__title">A post on your feed</p><p>Your friends see it. The sites that sell your details don't.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="g-compare__item">
        <span class="g-compare__icon g-compare__icon--brand" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d={star} /></svg></span>
        <div><p class="g-compare__title">A request to each site</p><p>Sent the way each site asks for it, and checked again later.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="g-stripe" aria-hidden="true"></div>
<section class="home-band home-band--alt" aria-labelledby="steps-title">
  <div class="home-wrap">
    <div class="home-head">
      <h2 id="steps-title">How it works, in 3 steps</h2>
      {/* "six short setup screens" = STEPS in src/freemyid/wizard/draft.py */}
      <p class="text-muted">Six short setup screens. Then it does the asking for you.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="home-steps" role="list">
      <li class="home-step g-step"><span class="home-step__num" aria-hidden="true">1</span><h3>Tell it who to look for</h3><p>A name, and the city and state you live in. That's it.</p></li>
      <li class="home-step g-step"><span class="home-step__num" aria-hidden="true">2</span><h3>It asks the sites to take you down</h3><p>It uses each site's own removal process. If a site needs you to tick "I'm not a robot", it shows you a card and you do it.</p></li>
      <li class="home-step g-step"><span class="home-step__num" aria-hidden="true">3</span><h3>It keeps checking</h3><p>Sites sometimes list people again. You see what is confirmed, what is waiting and what needs you.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-band" aria-labelledby="who-title">
  <div class="home-wrap home-split home-split--top">
    <div class="home-stack">
      <h2 id="who-title">Who buys your details?</h2>
      {/* source: docs/POSITIONING.md verified claims (lines 29, 30), sources in docs/MARKETING_COPY.md */}
      <div class="g-quotes">
        <p>A report to the Director of National Intelligence, made public in 2023, says US intelligence agencies buy commercially available data about Americans, and warns it can enable blackmail, stalking and harassment.</p>
        <p>A 2024 federal law bars data brokers from selling Americans' sensitive data to foreign adversaries, and a DOJ rule has restricted bulk transfers to countries of concern since April 2025.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="home-sources text-muted">Sources: ODNI Senior Advisory Group report on commercially available information (dated January 2022, released June 2023); Protecting Americans' Data from Foreign Adversaries Act of 2024 (Pub. L. 118-50); DOJ Data Security Program, 28 CFR Part 202. Free My ID removes listings from people-search sites. It does not stop government or overseas access.</p>
    </div>
    {/* source: /safety/#never-asks master list (WO-162) */}
    <div class="g-never" id="safe">
      <h2>What Free My ID will never ask for</h2>
      <ul class="home-list" role="list">
        <li><span aria-hidden="true"></span>Your Social Security number</li>
        <li><span aria-hidden="true"></span>Your bank or card details</li>
        <li><span aria-hidden="true"></span>A payment of any kind</li>
        <li><span aria-hidden="true"></span>Your full birthday</li>
        <li><span aria-hidden="true"></span>The password to your everyday email</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If something says it is us and asks, it isn't. Stop and ask someone you trust. <a href={url("safety/#never-asks")}>See the full list</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-band pt-0" aria-labelledby="parent-title">
  <div class="home-wrap grid gap-xl">
    <div class="g-parent">
      <div>
        <h2 id="parent-title">Helping a parent or grandparent?</h2>
        <p>Install it with them and sit beside them for the six setup screens. They type their own name to agree. Their details stay on their computer.</p>
      </div>
      <a class={primary} href={url("families/")}>Read the family guide</a>
    </div>
    <div class="g-limits">
      <h2>Honest limits</h2>
      <p>Free My ID works on people-search and data-broker sites. It does not change what Facebook or Google does with your account. "Removed" means removed from that one site, not from the whole internet. Sites can list you again, which is why it keeps checking. Some sites need you to do a step yourself.</p>
      <p><a href={url("guides/")}>Prefer to do it by hand? Read the free opt-out guides</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</Base>
